WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
President Paul! President Paul!

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.640
A couple years ago, Rand Paul ran for president,

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:06.580
and the media asked:

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.450
Has the libertarian moment finally arrived?

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.789
President Paul! President Paul!

00:00:11.789 --> 00:00:14.030
But Paul’s Presidential campaign went nowhere.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.280
Rand&nbsp;Paul shouldn’t even be on the stage,

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.089
he's number 11; he's got 1% in the polls.

00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:20.680
I had high hopes this was

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.800
going to be the libertarian moment.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.980
The crowd was cheering.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.480
[Applause]

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.400
We have come to take our country back

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.360
What happened?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.000
I would say that

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.480
either the people aren't ready or perhaps

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.780
the people in the Republican primary aren't ready.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.020
Since Trump was elected,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.500
federal spending has risen about half a trillion dollars.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.360
It doesn't mean some of us aren't fighting.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.140
It just means we're losing the battle.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.400
But I think there are a lot of battles you lose in

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.120
Washington that you may be winning the hearts

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.000
and minds of people who aren't in Washington.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.280
Are we winning hearts and minds?

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.500
That’s what I try to do with these videos,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.550
but I wouldn’t say that we’re winning.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.220
With socialism newly popular,

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.900
Senator Paul felt compelled to write this book

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.460
making the case against it.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.020
More on that in another video.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.240
But Paul says progress has been made,

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:13.080
and evidence of that is President Trump implementing

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.860
Senator Pauls’ free market ideas on healthcare

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.220
Let competition drive prices down.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:19.960
The President said, it’s a great idea!

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:23.220
Paul then tweeted that he’s proud to stand with

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.280
President Trump, that together we

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.740
“cut taxes, repealed regulations,

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.800
and put better judges on the court.”

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.060
The plan is to get out of endless wars

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.400
Paul also praised the president for saying he’d

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.890
bring our soldiers home

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.000
A very bold move from President Trump,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.350
it’s exactly what he promised the American people.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.200
Paul tweeted

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.160
"The first president to understand

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.800
what our national interest is."

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.420
But he hasn't pulled out of anywhere.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.200
Compare it though to George W. Bush,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.940
who got us involved everywhere.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.640
Or compared to President Obama,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.700
who sent 100,000 troops to Afghanistan.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.460
The rhetoric of President Trump has actually been,

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.980
I think, a relief.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.520
Bring our soldiers back home,

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.360
to not be policing agents all over the world.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.474
Has it happened yet?

00:02:05.474 --> 00:02:07.320
No, but I continue to push

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.759
We should get out of Afghanistan

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:10.940
But when the president has said anything about it,

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.280
when I have supported him, immediately

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.300
the Republican leaders and the Democrat leaders

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.500
get together and they hurry,

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:18.940
and they immediately pass a resolution saying

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.459
it would be precipitous to leave Afghanistan.

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:24.000
the danger of a precipitous withdrawal.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.140
Really after 19 years, precipitous?

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:27.960
[gunshot]

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.760
America went into Afghanistan to take out

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.920
the killers behind the September 11th attack.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:34.983
We did that,

00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:38.230
but we’re still there 18 years later.

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:39.240
You look at intervention,

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.640
after intervention, after intervention,

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.860
we haven't had the intended consequence.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.440
We've got more chaos

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.680
Chaos erupted at an American outpost in Afghanistan

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.320
In Iraq, we took out Saddam...

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.459
Saddam Hussein captured alive

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.400
But the people who replaced him were often worse...

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.300
We got rid of Ghaddafi the dictator,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.580
but what replaced him isn’t better.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.660
In Syria we armed rebels to fight Assad.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.500
But often our weapons ended up in the hands

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.440
of Al Qaeda –

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.900
Everything we think we're going to get more of,

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.440
stability or less terrorism,

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.849
we end up getting more chaos and more terrorism

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:14.700
So, President Trump is right, says Paul, when he says:

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.960
We want to bring our soldiers back home.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.860
Recently, Trump moved some troops

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:20.180
from northern Syria

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.740
He moved 50 out of the way

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.100
and all the war hawk caucus have gone crazy

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.639
Leaving the Kurds for slaughter!

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:29.220
This reckless action

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.219
This is the most screwed up decision I've

00:03:31.219 --> 00:03:32.880
seen since I've been in Congress

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.680
he had the audacity to move 50 soldiers.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.880
And it's like, these people are insane.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.730
A betrayal of the strongest allies

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:43.100
Four years ago, you said,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.560
"The United States should arm the Kurds.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.880
Promise them their own country.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.080
And now, those 50 soldiers were presumably

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.669
keeping the Turks from killing the Kurds.

00:03:53.669 --> 00:03:54.870
You've abandoned them.

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:56.820
When I refer to the Kurds having a homeland,

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.800
they kind of do.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.200
They have a of section of Iraq.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.260
I know they would wish it;

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.660
they would hope it to be a country.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.380
But I never really have advocated that we would

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.660
mandate or protect some sort of new country

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.520
within Syria for the Kurds.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.020
The bottom line is that the people who live there

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:10.980
know better about this

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.980
It's a very complicated war over there.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.520
There’s four or five different countries involved in it.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.420
We can't know enough about these problems.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.780
And unless you want to put 100,000 troops in there

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.860
and fight Assad, Russia, Turkey….

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.540
We ought to rethink whether we should get involved

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.780
in these wars to begin with.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.220
[Chopper Noise]

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.320
I promise you, 50 soldiers or 2000 American soldiers

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.940
are nothing more than a target for bad people

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.460
to kill or to maim,

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.600
which will get us drug into a bigger war.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:41.520
I don’t know whether Senator Rand is right about Syria.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:44.100
But 18 years of war in the Middle East,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.340
America’s longest war ever,

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.580
hasn’t done what our leaders said it would.

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:52.880
We need our troops. But we should use them sparingly.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:56.420
Only when we’re sure it benefits our defense.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.260
And if we go to war,

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:01.280
the Constitution says Congress must vote

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:02.440
to declare war.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.540
I’m glad Senator Paul argues those points.

